#question(title: [Intervals of monotonicity], centered: true)[
  Let
  $display(g(x) = x^3 (x^2 - 4)^(1 \/ 3) .)$

  Find out on which intervals this function
  is increasing or decreasing.

  Using that information, sketch its graph.

  To save time, here is the first derivative:
  $
    g' (x) = (x^2 (11 x^2 - 36))/(3(x^2 - 4)^(2 \/ 3))
  $
]
